<H1>Medium data</H1>
Search for medium no. = [236].
<HR>
Unless otherwise stated, sterilize media by autoclaving at 121&#176;C for 15 min.
<HR>
<P><B><FONT SIZE=3>236&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;THERMOCLADIUM MEDIUM</FONT></B></P>
<TABLE BORDER>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Modified Brock's salt base solution (see Medium No. <a href="/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=165">165</a>)   </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;1.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> L  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Trisodium citrate&#183;2H<sub>2</sub>O                         </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;2.94&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Yeast extract (BD-Difco)                                </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.5&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Trace vitamins (see Medium No. <a href="/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=197">197</a>)                  </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;10.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Resazurin                                               </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;1.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> mg  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Na<sub>2</sub>S&#183;9H<sub>2</sub>O                                   </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.5&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Sulfur (powder)                                        </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;10.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
Combine Modified Brock's salt base solution, trisodium citrate and resazurin, and adjust pH to 3.5 with 10 N H<sub>2</sub>SO<sub>4</sub>.  Autoclave under a N<sub>2</sub> atmosphere. Separately autoclave yeast extract and Na<sub>2</sub>S&#183;9H<sub>2</sub>O as 10% and 5% solutions, respectively, under a N<sub>2</sub> atmosphere. Filter-sterilize Trace vitamins.  Steam sulfur for 3 hr on each of 3 successive days.  Aseptically mix components except Na<sub>2</sub>S&#183;9H<sub>2</sub>O in suitable culture vessels (e.g., 20 ml of the medium in 120 ml serum bottles) while gassing with H<sub>2</sub>-CO<sub>2</sub> (80:20) gas mixture and seal with butyl rubber stoppers.  Prior to inoculation, aseptically and anaerobically add the Na<sub>2</sub>S&#183;9H<sub>2</sub>O solutions and adjust pH to 4.0-4.5, if necessary.  When the indicator (resazurin) turns to colorless, inoculate the culture and pressurize the vessels to 100 kPa H<sub>2</sub>-CO<sub>2</sub> (80:20).       <br>
